- Optimize input handling performance (no chug/lag),
- Make the 'compass' a compass,
- Chat panel?
- Right-click context menu with "Copy" or "Dictionary" for individual words?
- ResetClock: re-derive the FES-suppression model from the wire. The engine assumes
  a ~500ms server rate limit, but the corpus contradicts a time-based cause: 547
  stats-container pairs land <500ms apart, 58 under 250ms, and two probes sent in the
  same millisecond were both answered. Clio's FES.md says the score packet is sent
  when a stat CHANGES. If suppression is change-driven, every sample the engine
  discards as a "collision" is the server stating the value did not change - the most
  informative signal available to something whose whole job is finding the change
  instant. Also: LogResetDiagnostics defaults to false, so the theory currently cannot
  be falsified in normal use.
- Combat: DONE for the fight-end codes (2026-08-26). CombatTracker now reads 08 10/11/12
  as LineKind.FightEnd and treats it as authoritative that a fight ended even when no regex
  matches the wording. The question this item asked has an answer, and it is no: a FAILED
  flee carries the same 08 11 as a real one (19 occurrences, no exceptions), because 08 11
  is "fight ends - flee" - a REASON the fight ended, not a report of whether anyone got
  away. The one-word text distinction has no coded source and cannot be replaced. Measured
  table and the resulting rule ("the code carries the reason, the prose carries the
  particulars") in tools/combat/FIGHT-ENDS.md.
  Still open, same area: the 07 "isolated hit" family (bites/stings/kicks/throws) is
  unparsed, so a wyvern's venomous tail sting - real damage, its own code, its own
  "Stamina=N/M." line - is invisible to per-fight stats. See MECHANICS_NOTES.md.
